story=[]
def p(t,style='BodyX'):story.append(Paragraph(t,styles[style]))
def h(t):p(t,'HeadX')
def eq(t):p(t,'EqX')
def page():story.append(PageBreak())
def table(rows,widths):
 t=Table([[Paragraph(str(c),styles['SmallX']) for c in r] for r in rows],colWidths=widths,repeatRows=1,hAlign='LEFT')
 t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#e1edf6')),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('GRID',(0,0),(-1,-1),.4,colors.HexColor('#c3d2de')),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),8),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),8),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5)]));story.append(t);story.append(Spacer(1,10))
def question(n,points,steps,result,range_):
 h(f'Question {n} | {points} '+('point' if points==1 else 'points'))
 p(escape(qs[n]));eq(steps);p(f'<b>Answer:</b> {result}. <b>Accepted range:</b> {range_}.')
p('TEACHER GRADING GUIDE','SmallX')
p('Unit 1 Honors Lab','TitleX')
h('Mission Control Retro-Burn Landing')
p('Complete problems, worked solutions, and Section 5 grading procedures. Aligned to the current local Buzz question bank and flight model, reviewed October 10, 2026.')
h('Assessment at a glance')
p('<b>15 points total:</b> Questions 1-8 = 11 numeric points; Question 9 = 4 points for the program-generated Section 5 completion record. Section 5 is all-or-nothing.')
table([['Problem','Correct answer','Points','Accepted numeric range'],['1. Burn displacement','62.5 m','1','62.0 to 63.0'],['2. Cutoff velocity','+50 m/s','1','49.5 to 50.5'],['3. Coast displacement','125 m','2','124.0 to 126.0'],['4. Coast duration','5.0 s','1','4.90 to 5.10'],['5. Maximum height','187.5 m','2','186.5 to 188.5'],['6. Time to apex','7.5 s','1','7.40 to 7.60'],['7. Retro displacement','-62.5 m','1','-63.0 to -62.0'],['8. Retro duration','2.5 s','2','2.45 to 2.55'],['9. Parachute analysis','Depends on recorded flight','0 or 4','Times +/-0.10 s; percent +/-0.5 percentage points']],[139,131,43,191])
h('Fixed mission givens: Questions 1-8')
p('Start at rest on the pad: y = 0 m and v = 0 m/s. Upward is positive. Powered burn: net a = +20 m/s<super>2</super> for 2.5 s. Engine-off acceleration: -10 m/s<super>2</super>. Retro ignition occurs at one third of the apex height; its net acceleration is +20 m/s<super>2</super>, ending at rest on the pad.')
p('<b>Use the stated net accelerations.</b> Do not subtract gravity again during either powered burn. Use 10 m/s<super>2</super> for gravity, not 9.8. Section 5 uses different flight settings.','SmallX')
page();h('Sections 1-2 | Burn and coast')
question(1,1,'dy = v<sub>0</sub>t + (1/2)at<super>2</super><br/>= 0(2.5) + (1/2)(20)(2.5)<super>2</super><br/>= 10(6.25) = <b>62.5 m</b>','62.5 m','62.0-63.0 m')
question(2,1,'v = v<sub>0</sub> + at<br/>= 0 + (20)(2.5) = <b>+50 m/s</b>','+50 m/s, upward','49.5-50.5 m/s')
question(3,2,'v<sub>f</sub><super>2</super> = v<sub>i</sub><super>2</super> + 2a(dy)<br/>0 = 50<super>2</super> + 2(-10)(dy)<br/>dy = -2500 / -20 = <b>125 m</b>','125 m of additional height','124.0-126.0 m')
question(4,1,'v<sub>f</sub> = v<sub>i</sub> + at<br/>0 = 50 - 10t<br/>t = 50/10 = <b>5.0 s</b>','5.0 s after cutoff','4.90-5.10 s')
p('<b>Common distinction:</b> coast displacement excludes the powered burn. Coast time begins at engine cutoff, not at liftoff.','SmallX')
page();h('Sections 3-4 | Apex and retro burn')
question(5,2,'y<sub>max</sub> = dy<sub>burn</sub> + dy<sub>coast</sub><br/>= 62.5 + 125 = <b>187.5 m</b>','187.5 m above the pad','186.5-188.5 m')
question(6,1,'t<sub>apex</sub> = t<sub>burn</sub> + t<sub>coast</sub><br/>= 2.5 + 5.0 = <b>7.5 s</b>','7.5 s from liftoff','7.40-7.60 s')
question(7,1,'y<sub>ignition</sub> = y<sub>max</sub>/3 = 187.5/3 = 62.5 m<br/>dy<sub>retro</sub> = y<sub>final</sub> - y<sub>ignition</sub><br/>= 0 - 62.5 = <b>-62.5 m</b>','-62.5 m; downward displacement','-63.0 to -62.0 m')
question(8,2,'Before retro: dy = 62.5 - 187.5 = -125 m.<br/>v<sub>ignition</sub><super>2</super> = 0 + 2(-10)(-125) = 2500<br/>Choose the downward root: v<sub>ignition</sub> = -50 m/s.<br/>During retro: 0 = -50 + 20t; t = <b>2.5 s</b>','2.5 s from retro ignition to touchdown','2.45-2.55 s')
p('<b>Check:</b> (-50)(2.5) + (1/2)(20)(2.5)<super>2</super> = -62.5 m, matching Question 7. The 5.0 s free-fall interval before ignition is not part of the retro duration.','SmallX')
page();h('Section 5 | Question 9 and student prompts')
p('<b>Question 9 | 4 points | Hidden program-generated response</b>')
p(escape(qs[9]))
h('The four student-facing problems')
for label in ['Total time from liftoff to touchdown (s)','Time from parachute deployment to touchdown (s)','Parachute time as a percentage of total airborne time (%)','Was the landing safe (speed at most 6 m/s)?']:p('&bull; '+label)
h('Section 5 givens')
p('Start at rest. Net powered acceleration is +15 m/s<super>2</super>. The student chooses engine cutoff; fuel forces cutoff at 4.00 s. With the engine off and chute closed, a = -10 m/s<super>2</super>. The chute can open while descending at 5 m/s or faster.')
p('With the chute open, net a = +12 m/s<super>2</super> until velocity reaches -5 m/s; then descent continues at constant -5 m/s. A safe landing has touchdown speed at most 6 m/s. A late deployment may cause touchdown before steady descent begins.')
h('How to grade the completion record')
p('Award <b>4/4 only if all four answers are correct</b> for the attached completed flight with a deployed parachute. Otherwise award <b>0/4</b>. There is no partial credit. A hard landing can earn full credit when correctly analyzed.')
p('The hidden response begins <b>U1H_SECTION5_COMPLETE_V1</b> and includes JSON with status complete, maximum 4, the flight record, numeric answers, and tolerances. Check the recorded events and recompute the answers; the marker alone is not sufficient.')
p('Times must be within <b>0.10 s</b>; percentage must be within <b>0.5 percentage points</b>. Safety must match the magnitude of touchdown velocity. Blank, missing, inconsistent, or undeployed-flight evidence earns zero. Work in other sections cannot substitute.')
p('<b>Important:</b> the student sees rounded heights and velocities, not a flight timer. Use the attached event times to verify grading, and the phase equations on the next page to check the student\'s calculations.','SmallX')
page();h('Section 5 | General worked solution method')
p('Use the student\'s own completed flight. Let b be burn duration, v<sub>c</sub> cutoff velocity, v<sub>d</sub> deployment velocity (negative), y<sub>d</sub> deployment height, and v<sub>L</sub> touchdown velocity.')
h('1. Reconstruct phase times')
eq('Burn: t<sub>burn</sub> = b; v<sub>c</sub> = 15b<br/>Coast to apex: t<sub>coast</sub> = v<sub>c</sub>/10<br/>Fall from apex to deployment: t<sub>fall</sub> = |v<sub>d</sub>|/10')
p('For a flight that reaches steady descent, the velocity changes from v<sub>d</sub> to -5 m/s during braking:')
eq('t<sub>brake</sub> = (-5 - v<sub>d</sub>)/12<br/>y<sub>s</sub> = y<sub>d</sub> + v<sub>d</sub>t<sub>brake</sub> + 6t<sub>brake</sub><super>2</super><br/>t<sub>steady</sub> = y<sub>s</sub>/5')
p('If the rocket touches down before reaching -5 m/s, use the actual touchdown velocity instead. There is no steady-descent interval:')
eq('t<sub>brake</sub> = (v<sub>L</sub> - v<sub>d</sub>)/12; t<sub>steady</sub> = 0<br/>Alternatively solve 0 = y<sub>d</sub> + v<sub>d</sub>t + 6t<super>2</super><br/>and take the first nonnegative ground-crossing time.')
h('2. Solve the four requested answers')
table([['Student problem','Solution'],['Total airborne time','T = b + t<sub>coast</sub> + t<sub>fall</sub> + t<sub>brake</sub> + t<sub>steady</sub>'],['Deployment-to-touchdown time','C = t<sub>brake</sub> + t<sub>steady</sub>'],['Parachute-time percentage','P = 100(C/T)'],['Landing safety','Safe if |v<sub>L</sub>| is at most 6 m/s; otherwise hard.']],[163,341])
h('Independent check using the attached events')
p('T = Touchdown time - Liftoff time.<br/>C = Touchdown time - Parachute opens time.<br/>P = 100C/T. Do not start chute time at steady descent; braking already occurs with the chute open.')
p('Retain unrounded intermediate values. If the student uses the displayed two-decimal event data, allow the published tolerances. The following examples are teacher illustrations, not a universal answer key for every flight.','SmallX')
page();h('Section 5 | Fully worked safe-landing example')
p('<b>Example flight:</b> cut the engine at 2.00 s and open the chute at 55.00 m while descending at -20.00 m/s. This example was checked against the lab flight model.')
table([['Event','Height (m)','Velocity (m/s)','Time (s)'],['Liftoff','0','0','0'],['Engine cutoff','30','+30','2.000'],['Apex','75','0','5.000'],['Parachute opens','55','-20','7.000'],['Steady descent begins','39.375','-5','8.250'],['Touchdown','0','-5','16.125']],[177,95,120,112])
h('Calculate the intervals')
eq('Burn height = (1/2)(15)(2)<super>2</super> = 30 m; cutoff v = 15(2) = 30 m/s.<br/>Coast time = (0 - 30)/(-10) = 3.000 s.<br/>Coast rise = 30<super>2</super>/20 = 45 m; apex height = 30 + 45 = 75 m.<br/>Fall time = (-20 - 0)/(-10) = 2.000 s.<br/>Braking time = [-5 - (-20)]/12 = 1.250 s.<br/>Braking displacement = (-20)(1.25) + 6(1.25)<super>2</super> = -15.625 m.<br/>Steady-descent height = 55 - 15.625 = 39.375 m.<br/>Steady-descent time = 39.375/5 = 7.875 s.')
h('Answers to all four problems')
p('<b>Total time:</b> 2 + 3 + 2 + 1.25 + 7.875 = <b>16.125 s</b> (16.13 s rounded).')
p('<b>Parachute time:</b> 1.25 + 7.875 = <b>9.125 s</b> (9.13 s rounded).')
p('<b>Percentage:</b> 100(9.125/16.125) = <b>56.589%</b> (56.59% rounded).')
p('<b>Safety:</b> |-5| = 5 m/s, which is at most 6 m/s: <b>safe landing</b>.')
p('<b>Grading:</b> this flight earns 4/4 only with valid generated evidence and all four correct responses. Numerical answers from this example should not be applied to another student\'s flight.')
page();h('Section 5 | Fully worked hard-landing example')
p('<b>Example flight:</b> cut the engine at 2.00 s again, but wait until 5.00 m altitude to deploy. Burn and coast still take 2.00 s and 3.00 s; the apex is still 75.00 m.')
eq('Fall displacement = 5 - 75 = -70 m.<br/>v<sub>d</sub><super>2</super> = 2(-10)(-70) = 1400<br/>v<sub>d</sub> = -sqrt(1400) = -37.41657 m/s.<br/>Fall time = 37.41657/10 = 3.741657 s.<br/>Touchdown v<super>2</super> = v<sub>d</sub><super>2</super> + 2(12)(-5) = 1280<br/>v<sub>L</sub> = -sqrt(1280) = -35.77709 m/s.<br/>Braking time = [-35.77709 - (-37.41657)]/12 = 0.136624 s.')
p('The rocket hits the ground while still braking. Do not assume it reaches -5 m/s or add a steady-descent interval.')
p('<b>Total time:</b> 2 + 3 + 3.741657 + 0.136624 = <b>8.878281 s</b> (8.88 s).')
p('<b>Parachute time:</b> <b>0.136624 s</b> (0.14 s).')
p('<b>Percentage:</b> 100(0.136624/8.878281) = <b>1.538855%</b> (1.54%).')
p('<b>Safety:</b> 35.77709 m/s exceeds 6 m/s: <b>hard landing</b>. Correct analysis with valid completion evidence still earns 4/4.')
h('Teacher grading notes')
p('Use the published numeric ranges for Questions 1-8. Their original format requests numeric answers, not written derivations; the worked solutions in this guide support teacher review. Do not impose extra written-work requirements retrospectively.')
p('For manual review, accept equivalent methods and reasonable rounding. Credit consistent follow-through without repeatedly penalizing one original error. Section 5 remains binary. Do not award extra points for optional practice or a file upload.')
p('Common errors: using total height for coast height; adding burn time to coast-only time; omitting the negative sign in Question 7; using +10 rather than the net +20 for retro acceleration; reusing fixed-mission settings in Section 5; treating a negative landing velocity as automatically safe.')
h('Source and version notes')
p('Based on the current local files in unit-ApplicationFiles/unit-1/lesson-honors: buzz-assessment-questions.txt; u1h_rocket_launch_buzz_setup.txt; the Buzz assessment template; parachute-challenge.html; parachute-flight.js; and parachute-grading.js. The nine-question Buzz assessment is the grading authority; older standalone practice charts are not additional scored questions. Confirm the deployed assignment matches this version before grading.','SmallX')
